%I A398236 #15 Aug 01 2026 20:35:39
%S A398236 52551817,52551823,52551841,52561673,52561703,52561787,52561889,
%T A398236 52561987,52562017,52562021,52562443,52562483,52562509,52562527,
%U A398236 52562561,52562603,52562771,52565209,52565237,52566403,52566457,52566461,52567201,52567241,52567271,52567279,52567301
%N A398236 Primes p for which pi_{24;11,17}(p) - pi_{24;1,19}(p) = -1, where pi_{m;a,b,...}(x) is the number of primes <= x which are congruent to a or b or ... (mod m).
%C A398236 Let H be a proper subgroup of (Z/NZ)* containing all the squares, and S != H be a coset of H. Assuming the generalized Riemann hypothesis (GRH) and the Grand Simplicity Hypothesis (GSH; called LI in page 29 of Greg Martin's 2010 link), then pi_{N;S}(x) > pi_{N;H}(x) occurs more often than not: the set {pi_{N;S}(x) > pi_{N;H}(x)} has logarithmic density greater than 1/2. This phenomenon is called "Chebyshev's bias".
%C A398236 Here we have N = 24, H = {1,19} and S = {11,17}. The 27 known terms are all from a single sign-changing zone (52551817-52567301) of pi_{24;11,17} - pi_{24;1,19}. No furthur terms up to p = 1583717861701, for which pi_{24;11,17}(p) - pi_{24;1,19}(p) = 41997.
%H A398236 Greg Martin and Daniel Fiorilli, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Chennai-31Aug10.pdf">Prime number races: An asymptotic formula for the densities</a>, Analytic and Combinatorial Number Theory, Institute of Mathematical Sciences, Chennai, India. August 31, 2010.
%H A398236 Greg Martin, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Canberra-29Nov18.pdf">Prime number races</a>, Pure Math Seminar, UNSW Canberra. November 29, 2018.
%H A398236 Andrey S. Shchebetov, <a href="https://math101.guru/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/01-A3-Presentation-v7.3EN-no.pdf">Testing Chebyshev's bias for prime numbers up to 10^15</a>, EUCYS 2018.
%H A398236 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chebyshev%27s_bias">Chebyshev's bias</a>.
%o A398236 (PARI) my(k=0); forprime(p=2, 1e11, if(p%24==1||p%24==19, k--); if(p%24==11||p%24==17, k++); if(k==-1, print1(p, ", ")))
%Y A398236 Cf. other races between cosets of index 4 in (Z/24Z)*: A295354 (between {1,17} and {7,23}), A297448 (between {1,17} and {5,13}), A297355 (between {1,13} and {5,17}), A297357 (between {1,13} and {7,19}), A398234, A398235.
%K A398236 nonn,more
%O A398236 1,1
%A A398236 _Jianing Song_, Jul 24 2026
